  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Arie Stelloo is a Dutch entrepreneur who founded Issue Information Technology, a Rotterdam supplier of computer systems and related services. He made his fortune through the business's sale and later invested in Belgian property through Movast. Issue served corporate customers as well as organisations in government and education across the Netherlands.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 92,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Founder history, originating fortune, customers and later property participation agree across contemporary business reporting."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S1",
      "S2",
      "S3",
      "S4"
    ],
    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Arie Stelloo is a Dutch entrepreneur who founded Issue Information Technology, a Rotterdam supplier of computer systems and related services. He made his fortune through the business's sale and later invested in Belgian property through Movast. Issue served corporate customers as well as organisations in government and education across the Netherlands.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "When a stock-market listing was possible, Arie Stelloo chose private investment instead. In 1999, he preferred selling a majority stake in Issue to 3i over spending time answering shareholders' financial questions. The business had expanded from computer-aided design systems into networks, office automation and implementing SAP software.\n\nA later sale to Detron brought together businesses that already worked for customers jointly. Stelloo argued that clients wanted a local Dutch provider with a broader range of services. Issue contributed purchasing expertise, logistics and a public-tender team. Forehand, the connectivity wholesaler he had also founded, stayed outside that transaction.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 92,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Contemporary transaction reporting includes his explanation of both strategic decisions and the precise boundary of the later sale."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S2",
      "S3"
    ],
    "word_count": 97,
    "html": "<p>When a stock-market listing was possible, Arie Stelloo chose private investment instead. In 1999, he preferred selling a majority stake in Issue to 3i over spending time answering shareholders' financial questions. The business had expanded from computer-aided design systems into networks, office automation and implementing SAP software.</p>\r\n<p>A later sale to Detron brought together businesses that already worked for customers jointly. Stelloo argued that clients wanted a local Dutch provider with a broader range of services. Issue contributed purchasing expertise, logistics and a public-tender team. Forehand, the connectivity wholesaler he had also founded, stayed outside that transaction.</p>\r\n"
  },
